 "result": "**Emil Hansen** (Oslo). Their first order was a headset for \u20ac75.00 on 2026-11-05, the most expensive first order of any customer.\n\nFirst order for each customer:\n\n| Customer | First order | Total |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Emil Hansen** (Oslo) | Headset, 2026-11-05 | **\u20ac75.00** |\n| Ben Okafor (Lagos) | Mouse, 2026-08-19 | \u20ac45.00 |\n| Ana Costa | Desk lamp, 2026-08-14 | \u20ac39.00 |\n| Ben Okafor (Accra) | Cable, 2026-09-20 | \u20ac30.00 |\n| Chen Wei | USB hub (date unclear, see below) | \u20ac25.00 |\n| Dora Novak | Desk mat, 2026-07-21 | \u20ac19.00 |\n\nSome problems in the data, none of which change the answer:\n- **Inconsistent date format:** Chen Wei's USB hub order is dated `12/10/2026`, while every other date uses `YYYY-MM-DD`. I read it as 12 October, because 10 December would be after today. If it were December, Chen Wei's first order would be the \u20ac65 webcam instead, which is still less than \u20ac75.\n- **Missing total:** Emil Hansen's later order (keyboard stand, 2026-11-10) has no total. It isn't a first order, so it doesn't affect this result.\n- **Duplicate name:** There are two separate customers called Ben Okafor, one in Lagos and one in Accra. I counted them as different people.",
